# Counting Bits
# Idea: To count the number of 1 bits for each number in the range [0, num], we can use dynamic programming. We observe that the number of 1 bits in a number x is equal to the number of 1 bits in x // 2 plus the value of the lea…
# Line comments below keep the same logic as the NeetCode 150 repo solution.

class Solution:
    def countBits(self, num: int) -> List[int]:
        bits_count = [0] * (num + 1)

        for i in range(1, num + 1):
            bits_count[i] = bits_count[i // 2] + (i % 2)

        return bits_count
